{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_og3vpnutre54hja76wick6sgy2snicrtj2dqwyt3fdpmdt42ls6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything checks out. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Project structure:** `translated_rust/` contains a small C-to-Rust translation. The C side has one user-defined function `process_decisions(char*, size_t, int, int)` plus an entry-point `main`. There are **no Cargo features** in `Cargo.toml`, so there is exactly one valid configuration.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`Cargo.toml`** — added a `[lib] crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` so the Rust translation produces a shared library that exposes the same C ABI as the original. Added `libloading = \"0.8\"` to `[dev-dependencies]`.\n\n2. **`src/lib.rs`** — created with a `#[no_mangle] extern \"C\" fn process_decisions(...)` wrapper that mirrors the C contract (including the NULL-or-empty guard) and forwards to the existing pure-Rust `decisions` module. Also added `_init` and `_fini` no-op stubs (gated on `#[cfg(not(test))]`) to match the linker-generated stubs the C `.so` exports from `crti.o`/`crtn.o`.\n\n3. **`build.rs`** — added with a single `cargo:rustc-cdylib-link-arg=-nostartfiles` directive so our hand-written `_init`/`_fini` aren't double-defined by `crti.o`.\n\n4. **`src/main.rs`** — switched from `mod decisions;` to `#[path = \"decisions.rs\"] mod decisions;` so the `bin` doesn't depend on the rlib (which would import the `_init`/`_fini` stubs and conflict with `crti.o` during the `bin` link).\n\n5. **`tests/ffi_parity.rs`** — created an integration test that `dlopen`s both `c_src/build_so/libdriver_c.so` and `target/release/libdriver.so` via `libloading`, then drives `process_decisions` through every operation (0/1/2/3/invalid), every logic-op (0..3 + invalid), short/empty inputs, exhaustive small inputs (1..=4 chars over `{y,n,Y,N,?}`), the 32-element cap path, and various sequences exercising every `